From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:19:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: describe the CDSP as a cooling
 device

Add #cooling-cells to the CDSP so that thermal zones can throttle it
through its QMI TMD endpoints. The cooling devices appear once the CDSP
runs and offers its TMD service.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 903df4793533..ad1e43b42926 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -7635,6 +7635,8 @@
 			qcom,smem-states = <&smp2p_cdsp_out 0>;
 			qcom,smem-state-names = "stop";
 
+			#cooling-cells = <3>;
+
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			glink-edge {
